course: dictionary
lesson: 6710
title: One word, many meanings: off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word off is short, but it has lots of meanings. Each one depends on the words around it. «The TV is off» means it is not switched on. «I take one apple off the table» means I move it away from the table. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. If it is about a machine, a light or a tap, off probably means not working or not on. If it is about a place, a surface or a price, off probably means away from it or taken away. «She got 2 dollars off» means the price went down by 2 dollars.
explain: Off can also tell you about time and people. «I have a day off» means I am not at work or school that day. «She is off sick» means she is at home because she is ill. In each case, the words after off are the best clue.
fact: Off can be a preposition, an adverb or an adjective, so its job in a sentence can change.
fact: «Off» can mean away from a surface or a place, as in «take it off the table».
fact: «Off» can mean not working or not switched on, as in «the TV is off».
fact: «Off» can mean cancelled, as in «the match is off», and taken away from a price, as in «2 dollars off».
fact: «Off» can mean gone bad, as in «the milk is off», and it can mean away from work or school, as in «a day off».
exercise: «Take the cup off the table, please.» In this sentence, off means | not switched on | *away from the table | cancelled | taken off a price
exercise: «The TV is off.» What does off mean? | Away from work | Gone bad | Cancelled | *Not switched on
exercise: Jayden says, «I have a day off tomorrow.» What does off mean here? | Taken away from a price | Gone bad | *Away from work or school | Cancelled
test: «The match is off because of the rain.» In this sentence, off means | Not switched on | Away from a surface | *Cancelled | Taken off a price
test: «Ella got 2 dollars off the price of her ticket.» What does off mean here? | Not working | *Taken away from the price | Gone bad | Away from a place
exam: In formal writing, «20% off» could be written as | 20% gone bad | a rise of 20% | *a reduction of 20% | 20% extra
